# Blog Content Style

## No Em Dashes

**Never use em dashes (—) in blog posts.** Replace with commas, colons, parentheses, or separate sentences as appropriate.

### Examples

❌ **Bad:** "That initial impression shapes everything that follows—and often determines whether you get the deal."
✅ **Good:** "That initial impression shapes everything that follows, and often determines whether you get the deal."

❌ **Bad:** "By the time you call back—an hour later, end of day, next morning—they've moved on."
✅ **Good:** "By the time you call back (an hour later, end of day, or next morning), they've moved on."

❌ **Bad:** "Traditional tools—voicemail, static chatbots—weren't built for that reality."
✅ **Good:** "Traditional tools (voicemail, static chatbots) weren't built for that reality."

Use commas for simple breaks, parentheses for parenthetical phrases, and colons for introductions.
